1
00:00:01,480 --> 00:00:02,880
[片头主题曲响起]
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:02,920 --> 00:00:05,440
克拉克森：在今晚的《Top Gear》里，
CLARKSON: In tonight's Top Gear,

3
00:00:05,480 --> 00:00:08,200
超跑界的米克·贾格尔。
the Mick Jagger of supercars.

4
00:00:08,240 --> 00:00:12,920
我们将继续探寻全英国
哪个宗教跑得最快。
Our quest goes on to find Britain's
fastest faith.

5
00:00:12,960 --> 00:00:16,640
还有斯提格要收拾收拾TVR的新款轿跑。
And The Stig sorts out TVR's new coupe.

6
00:00:16,680 --> 00:00:18,920
[片头主题曲响起]
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

7
00:00:20,680 --> 00:00:23,240
大家好，热烈欢迎各位
Hello and a big yuletide welcome

8
00:00:23,280 --> 00:00:25,840
收看我们的《Top Gear》圣诞特辑。
to our festive edition of Top Gear.

9
00:00:25,880 --> 00:00:27,560
大家也看得出，我们省钱省到了极致。
As you can see, we spared every expense.

10
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:29,720
我们搞来了一根……圣诞树枝。
We've got a Christmas... twig.

11
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:31,200
[观众大笑]
还有，呃，
[AUDIENCE LAUGHING]
And, erm,

12
00:00:31,240 --> 00:00:34,440
几个橘子、一些坚果，还有，呃……噢！
some oranges and some nuts, and, er... oh!

13
00:00:34,480 --> 00:00:36,080
[观众大笑]
[AUDIENCE LAUGHING]

14
00:00:36,120 --> 00:00:38,280
一个圣诞彩球。
[观众鼓掌]
A bauble.
[AUDIENCE APPLAUDING]

15
00:00:40,240 --> 00:00:42,240
不不，我说啊，
听我说，
No, no, I tell you what,
I'll tell you what,

16
00:00:42,280 --> 00:00:43,920
咱们干脆把圣诞节
抛到脑后去，好不好？
let's just forget about
Christmas, shall we?

17
00:00:43,960 --> 00:00:48,120
来聊聊那些威风锃亮的大四驱。
Let's talk about big, shiny 4X4s.

18
00:00:48,160 --> 00:00:49,600
话说，买这种车的人，
Now, they tend to be bought,

19
00:00:49,640 --> 00:00:53,080
绝大部分其实都住在城里，
predominantly, by people who live in towns

20
00:00:53,120 --> 00:00:55,160
为的是下乡进村的时候，
so that when they go to the countryside

21
00:00:55,200 --> 00:00:57,520
自以为能融入当地。
they think they'll blend.

22
00:00:58,240 --> 00:00:59,600
真的吗？
Really?

23
00:00:59,620 --> 00:01:02,620
♪ 爱德华·埃尔加 - 《猎人》♪
♪ Edward Elgar - Nimrod ♪

24
00:01:03,520 --> 00:01:05,880
克拉克森：这就是乡下。
CLARKSON: This is the countryside.

25
00:01:05,920 --> 00:01:08,840
这地方又灰又土、粗砺沧桑，
It's a brown and gnarled place,

26
00:01:08,880 --> 00:01:11,440
跟住在这里的人一个德行。
much like the people who live in it.

27
00:01:13,080 --> 00:01:16,720
而这些就是乡下人开的车，
And these are the cars
that rural people drive,

28
00:01:16,760 --> 00:01:18,840
装了轮子的威灵顿雨靴。
Wellington boots with wheels.

29
00:01:18,880 --> 00:01:21,600
全是裹着泥巴的破烂玩意儿，全靠
Muddy, broken things that are held together

30
00:01:21,640 --> 00:01:23,960
稻草和死野鸡勉强拼凑在一起。
with straw and dead pheasants.

31
00:01:27,280 --> 00:01:30,080
在这儿……你很难融得进去，
It's... hard to blend here

32
00:01:30,120 --> 00:01:31,760
除非你本来就住这儿。
unless you live here.

33
00:01:36,560 --> 00:01:38,800
这是我的越野车。
This is my off-road car.

34
00:01:38,840 --> 00:01:41,840
一辆丰田陆地巡洋舰Amazon。
It's a Toyota Land Cruiser Amazon.

35
00:01:41,880 --> 00:01:45,320
它生来就是为了横扫
非洲和澳洲大地的，
And it's built to take on
Africa and Australia,

36
00:01:45,360 --> 00:01:47,040
所以早上在牛津郡
so it has no problem at all

37
00:01:47,080 --> 00:01:50,400
开着它送我孩子们上学，
那是轻轻松松、毫无压力。
taking my children to school
in the morning in Oxfordshire.

38
00:01:50,440 --> 00:01:51,640
它有七个座位，
It has seven seats,

39
00:01:51,680 --> 00:01:53,400
皮实耐造的内饰配件，
rough and tumble fixtures and fittings,

40
00:01:53,440 --> 00:01:56,960
而且开着它
总让人有一种所向披靡的感觉。
and there's a sense
of invincibility about it.

41
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:58,960
开着这车走在狭窄的乡间小道上，
When you drive this down a narrow road,

42
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:02,680
倒车让路的一定是对面那倒霉蛋。
it's the other guy who backs up.

43
00:02:02,720 --> 00:02:06,520
话说回来，你大可以开着这辆陆巡
去乡下打一天猎，
Now, you could use the Land Cruiser
for a day's shooting,

44
00:02:06,560 --> 00:02:08,440
但我劝你最好别这么干。
but I don't recommend it.

45
00:02:08,480 --> 00:02:11,120
倒不是说它越野不行。
它行得很，简直强得要命。
It's not that it doesn't work off-road.
It does. It's brilliant.

46
00:02:11,160 --> 00:02:14,600
纯粹是跟眼前的这幅画面，
怎么看怎么不搭调。
It just doesn't fit in
with the scene somehow.

47
00:02:14,620 --> 00:02:17,620
♪ Capella Istropolitana - Galliard A 5 ♪
♪ Capella Istropolitana - Galliard A 5 ♪

48
00:02:18,880 --> 00:02:21,600
你看，打猎是一项传统运动，
You see, shooting is a traditional sport

49
00:02:21,640 --> 00:02:23,240
赢家有野味当晚餐，
where the winner gets supper

50
00:02:23,280 --> 00:02:24,840
输家就只能饿肚子。
and the loser goes hungry.

51
00:02:24,880 --> 00:02:27,000
天地间只有你和你的猎枪，
There's just you and your piece

52
00:02:27,040 --> 00:02:28,760
以及整座森林的宁静。
and the stillness of the trees.

53
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:31,640
秋日篝火升起袅袅青烟，
Smoke curls from an autumnal fire,

54
00:02:31,680 --> 00:02:34,520
蒙蒙细雨润湿了万物的轮廓。
a gentle rain softens the edges.

55
00:02:37,560 --> 00:02:44,560
[枪声]
[GUNSHOTS]

56
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:48,240
而在这样一幅极具传统韵味的画卷里，
And in this traditional scene,

57
00:02:48,280 --> 00:02:50,360
这辆陆地巡洋舰未免显得太……
the Land Cruiser's just too...

58
00:02:50,400 --> 00:02:52,160
太俗气廉价了，总觉得不对味。
chintzy, somehow.

59
00:02:52,200 --> 00:02:54,680
我的意思是，瞧瞧，那才是纯正的绿色。
I mean, look, that is green.

60
00:02:54,720 --> 00:02:57,920
而那玩意儿，是丰田自以为的“绿”。
And that's Toyota's idea of "green".

61
00:02:58,840 --> 00:03:00,520
完全行不通。
It just doesn't work.

62
00:03:00,540 --> 00:03:02,700
♪ 贝多芬 - 第六交响曲：第一乐章 不太快的快板 ♪
♪ Ludwig van Beethoven -
Symphony No. 6: 1.
Allegro ma non troppo ♪

63
00:03:02,720 --> 00:03:05,440
宝马X5也同样让人绝望，
The BMW X5 is also hopeless,

64
00:03:05,480 --> 00:03:07,080
不过是出于完全不同的原因。
but for a different reason.

65
00:03:07,120 --> 00:03:10,600
没错，它块头够大；没错，
它也有四驱，
Yes, it's big and yes,
it has four-wheel drive,

66
00:03:10,640 --> 00:03:12,120
但也仅此而已了。
but that's the end of the story.

67
00:03:12,160 --> 00:03:14,760
它甚至连套越野胎都没配，
It doesn't even have off-road tyres,

68
00:03:14,800 --> 00:03:16,080
这感觉就像是跑到荒郊泥地里，
and that's like coming out here

69
00:03:16,120 --> 00:03:18,840
脚上却踩着一双Jimmy Choo高跟鞋。
in a pair of Jimmy Choo pumps.

70
00:03:20,560 --> 00:03:22,680
这车简直就是汽车界的“米利瓦尼利”……
This car is Milli Vanilli...

71
00:03:22,720 --> 00:03:26,880
纸面数据看着光鲜亮丽，
实际上纯粹是在假唱对口型。
looks good on paper,
but actually it's just miming.

72
00:03:26,900 --> 00:03:29,420
♪ Johnny Hawksworth - Roobarb ♪
♪ Johnny Hawksworth - Roobarb ♪

73
00:03:29,440 --> 00:03:32,120
哪怕是路况最平缓的泥道，
它都能陷进去，
On even the gentlest
of tracks, it gets stuck,

74
00:03:32,160 --> 00:03:35,440
接着驱猎员就会开着他那辆老路虎擦身而过，
and the beater will drive by
in his old Land Rover

75
00:03:35,480 --> 00:03:37,280
毫不留情地嘲笑你。
laughing at you.

76
00:03:37,320 --> 00:03:38,880
[狗叫声]
[DOG BARKING]

77
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:41,360
就算你是布兰福德侯爵，
也照样被笑话。
Even if you are
the Marquis of Blandford.

78
00:03:41,400 --> 00:03:44,000
刚才这幕是不是绝了？
Was that not perfect?

79
00:03:44,040 --> 00:03:46,480
那辆破路虎才值几个钱？30镑？
And how much is that
Land Rover worth? 30 quid?

80
00:03:46,520 --> 00:03:47,960
[笑声]
[LAUGHING]

81
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:51,800
行吧，不，我说句公道话，值200英镑。
Okay, no, I'll be fair, £200 worth.

82
00:03:51,840 --> 00:03:55,320
而那个呢，呃，值5万英镑，
结果陷在那儿动弹不得。
And that's, well, £50,000 worth
and it's stuck.

83
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:56,720
没错。
- 哪辆是你的？
That's right.
- Which is yours?

84
00:03:56,760 --> 00:03:57,640
男子：Trooper。
克拉克森：Trooper。
MAN: Trooper.
CLARKSON: Trooper.

85
00:03:57,680 --> 00:04:00,080
Trooper过得去吗？
- 也许吧，能行。
Trooper come by?
- Might. Yeah.

86
00:04:00,100 --> 00:04:03,100
♪ Johnny Hawksworth - Roobarb ♪
♪ Johnny Hawksworth - Roobarb ♪

87
00:04:15,080 --> 00:04:18,720
说来真邪门，那辆路虎跟我
同岁，
Very strangely, that Land Rover is exactly
the same age as me,

88
00:04:18,760 --> 00:04:20,640
而且是唯一爬上这个……
and is the only thing that's got up this...

89
00:04:20,680 --> 00:04:22,480
连我都爬不上这破坡！
I couldn't get up this hill!

90
00:04:22,520 --> 00:04:24,160
它身子骨比我还耐造！
It's lasted better than I have!

91
00:04:24,200 --> 00:04:26,520
男子：反正它比那辆宝马
爬得远。
MAN: It went further
than the BMW anyway.

92
00:04:26,560 --> 00:04:29,800
是啊，你赢了那台宝马……整整30英尺。
Yeah, you've beaten the BMW by... 30 feet.

93
00:04:29,840 --> 00:04:32,160
噢，好吧，
好歹能少走30英尺的路。
Oh, well,
that's 30 feet less to walk.

94
00:04:32,200 --> 00:04:33,760
[轻笑] 可不是嘛。
[CHUCKLES] Exactly.

95
00:04:33,780 --> 00:04:36,780
♪ John Cacavas - Bandits of the West ♪
♪ John Cacavas - Bandits of the West ♪

96
00:04:38,920 --> 00:04:41,880
那么，这台吉普大切诺基怎么样呢？
So, what about the Jeep Grand Cherokee?

97
00:04:41,920 --> 00:04:45,320
令人意外的是，作为一辆美国车，
它居然相当克制。
Surprisingly, for an American car,
it's quite restrained.

98
00:04:45,360 --> 00:04:48,400
它确实能融入
牛津郡的乡村风光，
It does blend in
to the Oxfordshire backdrop,

99
00:04:48,440 --> 00:04:51,840
而且在对付烂路泥泞时
也很有一套。
and it is good at dealing
with the rough stuff.

100
00:05:02,080 --> 00:05:04,520
但是，就算它在野外表现再好，
But, good though it may be out here,

101
00:05:04,560 --> 00:05:06,160
也还是有一两个毛病。
it does have one or two problems.

102
00:05:06,200 --> 00:05:08,400
开起来有一股浓浓的“农用车”质感。
It's quite agricultural-feeling.

103
00:05:08,440 --> 00:05:11,120
我倒不是太介意这点。
毕竟它是辆越野车嘛。
I don't really mind that.
I mean, it is an off-road car.

104
00:05:11,160 --> 00:05:15,640
我真正在意的是真皮座椅上
这些难看的褶皱，
What I do mind is the ruching
on the leather seats

105
00:05:15,680 --> 00:05:19,120
还有这恶心至极的塑料仿木饰板。
and this hideous fake plastic wood.

106
00:05:19,160 --> 00:05:21,920
而且这车里面的空间
It's also nowhere near as big on the inside

107
00:05:21,960 --> 00:05:25,120
也远没有你从外面看过去
所想象的那么大。
as you would imagine looking at it
from the outside.

108
00:05:25,160 --> 00:05:28,440
但这车最糟糕的一点，最要命的一点，
But the worst thing
about this, the worst thing,

109
00:05:28,480 --> 00:05:29,800
是你心里总会有一种感觉——
is that you've always got the sense

110
00:05:29,840 --> 00:05:32,400
自己买了个二流货。
that you've bought second best.

111
00:05:32,420 --> 00:05:35,420
♪ Edward Elgar - Nimrod ♪
♪ Edward Elgar - Nimrod ♪

112
00:05:49,160 --> 00:05:54,160
全新路虎揽胜
比吉普贵了整整两万英镑。
The new Range Rover
is £20,000 more than a Jeep.

113
00:05:54,200 --> 00:05:58,240
如今的它与其说是一辆车，
倒不如说是一艘豪华游艇。
These days it's more
a luxury yacht than a car.

114
00:05:58,280 --> 00:05:59,640
但别担心。
But don't worry.

115
00:05:59,680 --> 00:06:01,760
它骨子里依然能野能豁。
It can still play rough.

116
00:06:05,600 --> 00:06:07,200
好了，看好了。
Okay, look at this.

117
00:06:07,240 --> 00:06:09,040
我拨动这边的开关，
I flick this switch here

118
00:06:09,080 --> 00:06:12,840
开启陡坡缓降控制。
to engage the hill descent control.

119
00:06:12,880 --> 00:06:15,760
挂入空挡，切换到低速四驱。
Put it into neutral, engage low range.

120
00:06:15,800 --> 00:06:19,360
[叮声]
挂回前进挡，现在……
[DINGS]
Back into drive, and now...

121
00:06:20,680 --> 00:06:22,560
我只需把车头对准这里
I just point it at this

122
00:06:22,600 --> 00:06:25,360
看似根本下不去的陡坡……
seemingly impossible slope here...

123
00:06:26,080 --> 00:06:29,880
[兴奋地发笑并闷哼]
[LAUGHS AND GRUNTS IN ANTICIPATION]

124
00:06:30,280 --> 00:06:32,840
接下来我要干一件你们可能会觉得疯了的事。
And now I'm gonna do something you might
think is mad.

125
00:06:32,880 --> 00:06:36,000
我要把脚从刹车踏板上拿开。
I'm gonna take my foot off the brake.

126
00:06:36,040 --> 00:06:37,000
瞧好了？
Okay?

127
00:06:37,020 --> 00:06:40,020
♪ Edward Elgar - Nimrod ♪
♪ Edward Elgar - Nimrod ♪

128
00:06:41,360 --> 00:06:43,400
太绝了。
That's astonishing.

129
00:06:43,440 --> 00:06:46,960
我能感觉到防抱死刹车系统
正在轮流咬住各个车轮，
I can feel the anti-lock brakes
grabbing each of the wheels in turn,

130
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:49,880
确保车身笔直前进，
making sure that we stay straight.

131
00:06:49,920 --> 00:06:54,240
而且让我们始终保持步行的速度，
And that we continue to do a walking pace

132
00:06:54,280 --> 00:06:56,080
一路稳稳滑到山脚。
all the way down the hill.

133
00:06:59,400 --> 00:07:01,360
当然了，宝马X5也办得到这一点。
Now, of course, the X5 can do that as well.

134
00:07:01,400 --> 00:07:04,640
X5同样配有陡坡缓降控制系统。
The X5 also has a hill descent control.

135
00:07:04,680 --> 00:07:09,400
那是宝马当年掌管罗孚时顺手偷去的玩意儿。
It's something BMW stole while they were
running Rover.

136
00:07:09,440 --> 00:07:11,560
但X5做不到的，
But what the X5 can't do

137
00:07:11,600 --> 00:07:15,120
是掉个头再从这个坡上爬回去。
is turn round and go back up the slope.

138
00:07:15,160 --> 00:07:18,720
瞧，它没有低速分动箱，
See, it doesn't have a low-range gearbox.

139
00:07:18,760 --> 00:07:20,680
没有差速锁，
It doesn't have locking diffs.

140
00:07:20,720 --> 00:07:22,720
没有这大家伙的离地间隙，
It doesn't have this thing's
ground clearance

141
00:07:22,760 --> 00:07:24,400
也没有这么强的悬挂行程。
or wheel articulation.

142
00:07:24,440 --> 00:07:27,160
它根本算不上一台正经的越野车。
It's not a proper off-road car.

143
00:07:27,200 --> 00:07:28,880
而眼前这台揽胜，绝对是。
And this just is.

144
00:07:28,900 --> 00:07:31,220
♪ Capella Istropolitana - I. Prelude ♪
♪ Capella Istropolitana - I. Prelude ♪

145
00:07:31,240 --> 00:07:33,040
而且还有一点。
There's something else, too.

146
00:07:33,080 --> 00:07:36,120
路虎揽胜停在萨伏伊酒店门前固然气派，
A Range Rover looks good outside the Savoy.

147
00:07:36,160 --> 00:07:39,040
但在这荒郊野外，看着才更对味。
But it looks even better out here.

148
00:07:47,120 --> 00:07:49,440
话说当年，确实曾有那么一段时期，
Now, there was a time when Range Rovers

149
00:07:49,480 --> 00:07:52,200
揽胜是“货真价实”的越野之王。
WERE king off-the-road.

150
00:07:52,240 --> 00:07:55,320
如今它们身上依旧笼罩着一种不可战胜的光环，
And they still have an air
of invincibility about them,

151
00:07:55,360 --> 00:07:57,560
但相信我，
but believe me,

152
00:07:57,600 --> 00:08:00,360
你照样能把这玩意儿开陷车。
you can still get these things stuck.

153
00:08:01,040 --> 00:08:02,400
而且陷得死死的。
Really stuck.

154
00:08:02,420 --> 00:08:04,420
♪ Amilcare Ponchielli -
Dance of the Hours ♪
♪ Amilcare Ponchielli -
Dance of the Hours ♪

155
00:08:04,440 --> 00:08:06,200
明白我啥意思了吧？
