892
00:39:47,680 --> 00:39:50,720
两万两千四百镑，性价比相当高。
£22,400, that's seriously good value.

893
00:39:50,760 --> 00:39:53,160
汪克尔转子引擎，对开式“自杀后门”。
Wankel engine, suicide back doors.

894
00:39:53,200 --> 00:39:55,400
哈蒙德：不过说到那种
转子引擎吧，
HAMMOND: The thing about
those Wankel engines, though,

895
00:39:55,440 --> 00:39:57,320
以前一直有个大毛病。
they used to have a big problem.

896
00:39:57,360 --> 00:39:59,000
因为引擎深处有个叫
转子顶点密封片的东西，
'Cause it was something called the
rotor tips deep inside the engine,

897
00:39:59,040 --> 00:40:01,120
磨损得实在太快了，对吧？
they used to wear out
much too quickly, didn't they?

898
00:40:01,160 --> 00:40:03,080
克拉克森：嗯。
- 所以我觉得他们大概会换成……
CLARKSON: Mmm.
- So, I think they're gonna replace them...

899
00:40:03,120 --> 00:40:04,640
不，他们已经解决了。
No, they've solved that.

900
00:40:04,680 --> 00:40:07,520
他们用上了人类已知
最坚硬的物质。
They're using the hardest
substance known to man.

901
00:40:07,560 --> 00:40:09,440
钻石？
- 不，比钻石还硬。
Diamond.
- No, harder than diamonds.

902
00:40:09,480 --> 00:40:11,640
我来告诉你人类已知最硬的物质
到底是什么，
I'll tell you what the hardest substance
known to man is,

903
00:40:11,680 --> 00:40:13,080
他们拿什么来包覆转子顶点的。
what they're lining the rotor tips with.

904
00:40:13,120 --> 00:40:14,760
是维多麦麦片……
It's Weetabix...

905
00:40:14,800 --> 00:40:16,040
[观众笑声]
[AUDIENCE LAUGHING]

906
00:40:16,080 --> 00:40:17,480
听我把话说完，
Bear with me on this,

907
00:40:17,520 --> 00:40:19,440
就是那种泡在麦片碗里
没吃干净，
Weetabix that's been
left in the cereal bowl

908
00:40:19,480 --> 00:40:21,240
然后直接扔进洗碗机里的维多麦。
and then put in the dishwasher.

909
00:40:21,280 --> 00:40:22,480
[观众笑声]
[AUDIENCE LAUGHING]

910
00:40:22,520 --> 00:40:24,840
你试过把它抠下来吗？
Have you ever tried to get it off?

911
00:40:24,880 --> 00:40:26,840
毫无办法。
- 哦，这我信。那绝对顶用。
Nothing.
- Oh, I'll buy that. That would do it.

912
00:40:26,880 --> 00:40:30,240
我曾往碗里塞过60吨TNT想把它炸掉，
I have put 60 tons of TNT into the bowl
to get it out,

913
00:40:30,280 --> 00:40:32,080
碗都炸成碎渣了，
blew the bowl to smithereens,

914
00:40:32,120 --> 00:40:33,640
它还死死粘在碎片上！
still stuck to the pieces.

915
00:40:33,680 --> 00:40:35,200
绝对顶用，毫无疑问。
That would do it. No doubt about it.

916
00:40:35,240 --> 00:40:37,600
所以他们用的就是这玩意儿。
马自达维多麦。
So, that's what they're using.
It's the Mazda Weetabix.

917
00:40:37,640 --> 00:40:40,320
明年到底有没有那种……你知道的，
正经靠谱的家用车？
Are there any really like, you know,
sensible cars coming next year?

918
00:40:40,360 --> 00:40:42,960
呃，我手头正好有一份即将上市的
新车清单，
Well, I've got a list actually of the cars
that are coming in,

919
00:40:43,000 --> 00:40:45,840
而对你这个问题的回答
呢，呃，“并没有”。
and the answer to your question
is, erm, "Not really".

920
00:40:45,880 --> 00:40:47,720
呃，保时捷……
Erm, Porsche,

921
00:40:47,760 --> 00:40:52,200
额，他们造了辆卖五万英镑、
极速能跑150英里的越野车。
uh, they've made a £50,000,
150 mph off-roader.

922
00:40:52,240 --> 00:40:54,120
哈蒙德：一点都不务实。
克拉克森：确实不务实。
HAMMOND: Not sensible.
CLARKSON: That's not sensible.

923
00:40:54,160 --> 00:40:57,120
大众汽车，众所周知，
名字的意思就是“人民的汽车”。
Volkswagen, which, as we all know,
means "people car".

924
00:40:57,160 --> 00:40:59,640
结果他们造了辆卖六万英镑的辉腾。
They've made a £60,000 Phaeton.

925
00:40:59,680 --> 00:41:01,720
“人民之车。”
- 呵，这可真“务实”！
"People's car."
- Oh, that's sensible!

926
00:41:01,760 --> 00:41:05,040
人民之车。看来德国的经济状况
显然比咱们预想的要景气得多啊。
People's car. The economy's
obviously better in Germany
than we thought.

927
00:41:05,080 --> 00:41:06,760
噢，其实还真有一辆！
Oh, there is one, actually!

928
00:41:06,800 --> 00:41:10,760
还真有那么一辆务实的车，
沃克斯豪尔 Signum。
There is one sensible car,
the Vauxhall Signum.

929
00:41:10,800 --> 00:41:13,120
话说，这车骨子里其实就是辆威达。
Now, it's basically a Vectra.

930
00:41:13,160 --> 00:41:15,400
哎哟，我都困得直打瞌睡了！我真是太……
[观众大笑]
Oh, I'm nodding off! I'm just so...
[AUDIENCE LAUGHING]

931
00:41:15,440 --> 00:41:17,600
别别，我清醒过来了，我缓过来了。
No, no, I'm coming back. I'm coming back.

932
00:41:17,640 --> 00:41:19,520
我缓过来了。
[嗤笑]
I'm back.
[SNICKERING]

933
00:41:19,560 --> 00:41:22,360
咱们可不能被它的“威达味儿”给吓退了，
We mustn't be put off by its Vectraness

934
00:41:22,400 --> 00:41:25,560
因为它不像赛飞利，
赛飞利那玩意儿就像是辆七座版的雅特。
because it's not like a Zafira
which is the sort of seven-seat Astra.

935
00:41:25,600 --> 00:41:27,720
它只有五个座位。
It only has five seats.

936
00:41:27,760 --> 00:41:31,520
但据说后排的座椅全都能
前后挪动、往后斜靠什么的。
But, apparently, the ones in the back all
move about and recline and things.

937
00:41:31,560 --> 00:41:33,640
后排那些座椅，
设计得确实非常巧妙。
They're really clever,
the ones at the back.

938
00:41:33,680 --> 00:41:35,800
这绝对会成为有史以来第一辆
It's gonna be the first car ever

939
00:41:35,840 --> 00:41:37,880
大家争着抢着要坐后排的车。
where people will be fighting
to get in the back.

940
00:41:37,920 --> 00:41:40,960
“不不，你来开！
真的，前排归你了。
"No, no, you drive!
really, you have the front.

941
00:41:41,000 --> 00:41:43,160
你来开吧，我坐后头就好。
[全场大笑]
You drive it. I'll sit back here.
[ALL LAUGHING]

942
00:41:43,200 --> 00:41:45,440
太感谢了啊。”
“贴了深色车窗膜，谁也认不出我在这车里。”
Thanks very much."
Tinted windows, no one will know I'm in it.

943
00:41:45,480 --> 00:41:47,760
总之，新闻播送完毕。
Anyway, here endeth the news.

944
00:41:47,800 --> 00:41:49,520
啊，其实还没完呢，
Ah, no, it doesn't,

945
00:41:49,560 --> 00:41:53,480
因为 TVR 这家公司，大概每隔三周
就要推出一款新车，
because TVR, they launch a new car
about every three weeks

946
00:41:53,520 --> 00:41:55,040
而且每款车基本上都大差不差。
and they're all pretty much the same.

947
00:41:55,080 --> 00:41:57,600
这辆是 T350C，他们最新的力作。
This is the T350C, their latest offering.

948
00:41:57,640 --> 00:41:59,640
我甚至连看都不用看，
就知道会是副什么德行。
And without even looking
I know what I'm gonna get.

949
00:41:59,680 --> 00:42:02,760
肯定有极其性感、曼妙的曲线车身。
（理查德，你没事吧？）
There'll be a really sexy, curvy body.
(Richard, are you ok?)

950
00:42:02,800 --> 00:42:05,240
肯定配了一台声浪极为销魂的引擎，
It'll have a glorious sounding engine

951
00:42:05,280 --> 00:42:06,720
而且只有两个座位。
and there'll be two seats.

952
00:42:06,760 --> 00:42:08,640
瞧！果不其然。
Boom! And there it is.

953
00:42:08,680 --> 00:42:11,240
但问题在于，会买这辆车的
Thing is though this car is gonna be bought

954
00:42:11,280 --> 00:42:13,040
绝大部分都是赛道日发烧友。
largely by track day enthusiasts.

955
00:42:13,080 --> 00:42:15,480
你懂的，就是那种
能在周六把这车往死里虐、
You know, the kind of people
who'll thrash the bottom off it

956
00:42:15,520 --> 00:42:16,800
在赛道上豁得底朝天的人，
on a Saturday around the circuit,

957
00:42:16,840 --> 00:42:18,720
到了周一却还要开着它去通勤上班。
and then commute in it on a Monday.

958
00:42:18,760 --> 00:42:21,520
所以，它必须像化身博士一样，具备双重人格。
So, it needs to be a Jekyll and Hyde car.

959
00:42:21,560 --> 00:42:23,080
而想做到这一点，可绝非易事。
And that ain't easy.

960
00:42:23,100 --> 00:42:26,100
♪ 莱·库德 - 《德州巴黎》 ♪
♪ Ry Cooder - Paris, Texas ♪

961
00:42:29,200 --> 00:42:30,520
[轮胎尖叫声]
[TYRES SCREECHING]

962
00:42:33,000 --> 00:42:36,240
哈蒙德：这台新车搭载了TVR那台
久经考验的Speed Six发动机。
HAMMOND: The new car uses TVR's
proven speed six engine.

963
00:42:36,280 --> 00:42:38,680
能爆发出350匹马力，
It's good for 350 bhp

964
00:42:38,720 --> 00:42:42,800
能在4.4秒内
将这台T350推到时速60英里。
and will take the T350
to 60 mph in 4.4 seconds.

965
00:42:42,840 --> 00:42:45,160
它是硬顶而不是软顶敞篷，
It's a hard rather than a soft top,

966
00:42:45,200 --> 00:42:46,880
这让车身刚性更强。
and that makes it stiffer.

967
00:42:46,920 --> 00:42:49,440
那些车身线条在设计时，
And those curves were designed
with aerodynamics

968
00:42:49,480 --> 00:42:51,240
也是把空气动力学摆在第一位。
at the top of the priority list.

969
00:42:51,280 --> 00:42:55,080
无论在公路上还是赛道上，
这全都是大好消息。
All of which is good news,
both on the road and the track.

970
00:42:57,600 --> 00:43:00,320
但真正棘手的地方
在于底盘调校，
But where it gets a bit tricky
is the set-up,

971
00:43:00,360 --> 00:43:04,040
悬挂、底盘、
避震阻尼、弹簧，所有这些……
the suspension, the chassis,
dampers, springs, all of the...

972
00:43:04,080 --> 00:43:06,600
这堆让人头疼的玩意儿，
必须调得恰到好处。
All of this kind of caper.
Got to get it right.

973
00:43:08,320 --> 00:43:09,720
这里是赛道，
This is a track,

974
00:43:09,760 --> 00:43:11,880
铺着平整光滑的柏油路面，
covered in smooth, flat tarmac,

975
00:43:11,920 --> 00:43:14,840
所以悬挂你爱调多硬就调多硬，
so you can set the suspension up
to be as hard as you like

976
00:43:14,880 --> 00:43:15,920
只管刷出飞快的圈速。
to get a quick lap.

977
00:43:15,960 --> 00:43:17,640
[疾驰呼啸声]
[ZOOMING]

978
00:43:18,480 --> 00:43:20,600
但这边可是英国的马路，
But this is a British road,

979
00:43:20,640 --> 00:43:22,680
现实生活里，大家周一到周五开的日常路。
real life, the Monday-to-Friday road.

980
00:43:22,720 --> 00:43:25,520
糊弄事的修补路面、坑洼、颠簸、烂泥，
Shoddy repairs, lumps, bumps, mud,

981
00:43:25,560 --> 00:43:27,920
边上还缀满了一条条排水沟。
and all garnished with ditches.

982
00:43:27,960 --> 00:43:29,920
[引擎怠速声]
[ENGINE IDLING]

983
00:43:29,960 --> 00:43:32,840
于是，TVR运来了车，
外加一帮机械师。
So, TVR brought the car
and a clutch of mechanics.

984
00:43:32,880 --> 00:43:35,480
我们又叫来了斯提格，
他也掺和进来发表了自己的高见，
We added The Stig
who chucked in his ten-penneth

985
00:43:35,520 --> 00:43:37,400
帮着按他自己的口味把车调了一遍。
and helped set it up to his liking.

986
00:43:39,080 --> 00:43:40,440
[引擎轰鸣]
[ENGINE REVVING]

987
00:43:40,460 --> 00:43:43,040
♪ The Cardigans - My Favourite Game ♪
♪ The Cardigans - My Favourite Game ♪

988
00:43:43,040 --> 00:43:45,800
起步弹射时车尾居然连沉都不沉一下。
The car doesn't even sit down
when it leaves the line.

989
00:43:49,720 --> 00:43:51,680
看看这个，过弯姿态平得像块铁板，
And look at that, it corners dead flat,

990
00:43:51,720 --> 00:43:54,360
车身完全没有任何侧倾。
there's absolutely no body roll at all.

991
00:43:54,400 --> 00:43:56,240
而且速度极快。
And it's very fast.

992
00:43:56,280 --> 00:43:59,880
做出了1分28秒的漂亮圈速。
And a good lap time of 1:28.

993
00:43:59,920 --> 00:44:02,360
但在这个过程中，
他把这车搞得神经兮兮、
But in the process,
he's made the car twitchy,

994
00:44:02,400 --> 00:44:04,120
紧绷狂暴，一股斯提格的疯癫味。
edgy and Stig-like.

995
00:44:05,200 --> 00:44:06,720
完全游走在失控边缘。
Right on the limit.

996
00:44:06,760 --> 00:44:08,240
[轮胎尖叫]
[TYRES SCREECH]

997
00:44:26,120 --> 00:44:29,080
而当你离开赛道开车回家时，
噩梦才真正开始。
And it gets worse when you leave the track
to drive home.

998
00:44:30,440 --> 00:44:33,680
我觉得斯提格还是老老实实开车算了，
I think The Stig should stick
to driving cars,

999
00:44:33,720 --> 00:44:36,200
可别瞎折腾调校了。
rather than messing about with them.

1000
00:44:36,240 --> 00:44:40,720
因为这玩意儿开在公路上
简直遭罪透顶！
Because this is absolutely
awful on the road!

1001
00:44:40,760 --> 00:44:44,000
[轻笑] 这……这也太颠、太受罪了。
[CHUCKLING] It's... it's so uncomfortable.

1002
00:44:44,040 --> 00:44:47,240
而且不仅是受罪，
我……我根本没法控制转向！
And not just uncomfortable,
I... I can't steer!

1003
00:44:47,280 --> 00:44:48,960
我完全不知道
I really have no idea

1004
00:44:49,000 --> 00:44:50,760
下一秒它会往哪个方向窜。
which direction we're gonna go in next.

1005
00:44:50,800 --> 00:44:52,400
纯粹是随机乱撞。
It's just random.

1006
00:44:54,920 --> 00:44:56,400
所以只能回维修区，
So it's back to the pits,

1007
00:44:56,440 --> 00:44:59,240
让斯提格认清一下现实生活，
and The Stig is told
to get a grip on real life

1008
00:44:59,280 --> 00:45:03,520
帮TVR把这台350调校得
能让我们正常人也能开。
and help TVR set the 350 up
so that we can all use it.

1009
00:45:11,800 --> 00:45:13,440
接着重新驶上赛道，
And then it's back out onto the track

1010
00:45:13,480 --> 00:45:15,400
悬挂调校稍微偏软了一点。
with slightly softer settings.

1011
00:45:18,240 --> 00:45:20,000
[引擎加速轰鸣]
[ENGINE ACCELERATING]

1012
00:45:20,040 --> 00:45:21,560
[轮胎尖叫]
立马就能看出，
[TYRES SCREECHING]
And straightaway, you can see

1013
00:45:21,600 --> 00:45:23,000
车身晃动变多了，
there's more movement from the body,

1014
00:45:23,040 --> 00:45:24,960
过弯时的侧倾也更明显。
more body roll through the corners.

1015
00:45:25,000 --> 00:45:27,480
没错，圈速确实慢了整整一秒，
And, yes, the time
is actually a second slower

1016
00:45:27,520 --> 00:45:29,560
单圈成绩是1分29秒。
at 1:29 for the lap.

1017
00:45:29,600 --> 00:45:31,240
但依然是个非常漂亮的成绩，
But that's still a very good time.

1018
00:45:31,280 --> 00:45:32,760
而且车身动态容易捉摸多了。
And it's a lot more predictable.

1019
00:45:35,720 --> 00:45:37,520
开上普通公路，感觉好太多了，
Out on the road, it's much better.

1020
00:45:37,560 --> 00:45:39,440
更顺手，也更好开了。
More usable and drivable.

1021
00:45:39,480 --> 00:45:42,760
真要在现实路况里，它甚至比原先更快。
If anything, it's faster in the real world.

1022
00:45:42,800 --> 00:45:45,200
剩下的收尾工作就交由TVR自己解决吧。
We'll let TVR finish the job off.

1023
00:45:45,240 --> 00:45:47,640
[轮胎尖叫]
但至少现在他们心里有数，
知道极限在哪儿了。
[TYRES SCREECH]
But at least now they know
where the limit is.

1024
00:45:53,160 --> 00:45:56,480
关于这辆车，我有一件事非做不可，好吗？
There's one thing I want
to do with this car, okay?

1025
00:45:56,520 --> 00:45:58,280
就是给它想个像样点的名字。
Think of a better name for it.

1026
00:45:58,320 --> 00:46:01,160
T350C听着跟个电熨斗型号似的。
T350C sounds like an iron.

1027
00:46:01,200 --> 00:46:02,640
没错，听着就像后面带个电插头的玩意儿。
Yeah, whatever it is,
it's got a plug on it.

1028
00:46:02,680 --> 00:46:05,360
简直是个家用电器，所以绝对不行。
It's an appliance, so it won't do.

1029
00:46:05,400 --> 00:46:07,000
所以不管咱们想出什么名儿，
So, whatever we come up with,

1030
00:46:07,040 --> 00:46:09,400
就算厂方硬要叫它T350C，
even if they do call it a T350C,

1031
00:46:09,440 --> 00:46:11,200
我们也一律按咱们起的名字来叫。
- 这很公平。
we're gonna call it what we come up with.
- That's fair.

1032
00:46:11,240 --> 00:46:14,160
不过说真的，起名字这事儿其实相当棘手，对吧？
And actually choosing the name,
it can be quite tricky, okay?

1033
00:46:14,200 --> 00:46:16,560
我手里有一份清单，
上面列了几个“绝妙”的车名，
I mean, I've got a list here
of some of the better ones

1034
00:46:16,600 --> 00:46:19,760
而且全都是如假包换的真名字。
我发誓绝对没瞎编。
and these are all genuine.
I promise they're genuine.

1035
00:46:19,800 --> 00:46:22,680
比如：马自达“邦戈好朋友”（Bongo Friendee）。
There was the Mazda Bongo Friendee.

1036
00:46:22,720 --> 00:46:24,320
[观众大笑]
- 相当有品位。
[AUDIENCE LAUGHING]
- Very chic.

1037
00:46:24,360 --> 00:46:25,680
那这个呢？
How about this one?

1038
00:46:25,720 --> 00:46:29,200
三菱“迷你活力城市凉鞋”（Mini Active Urban Sandal）。
The Mitsubishi Mini Active Urban Sandal.

1039
00:46:29,240 --> 00:46:30,480
[观众大笑]
[AUDIENCE LAUGHING]

1040
00:46:30,520 --> 00:46:32,600
那这车标得做多大才写得下啊？
[窃笑]
How big was the badge?
[TITTERS]

1041
00:46:32,640 --> 00:46:34,440
或者说，这一辆才是全场最绝的。
Or, this is the best of the lot.

1042
00:46:34,480 --> 00:46:37,840
五十铃“神秘多功能巫师”（Isuzu Mysterious Utility Wizard）。
The Isuzu Mysterious Utility Wizard.

1043
00:46:37,880 --> 00:46:40,320
[观众笑声]
这名字太神了！
[AUDIENCE LAUGHING]
That's a superb name!

1044
00:46:40,360 --> 00:46:42,760
这都是些什么鬼名字？
- 而且还真不单是日本人这样。
What is that?
- And it's not just the Japanese either.

1045
00:46:42,800 --> 00:46:44,720
早在80年代，大众就推出过
Back in the '80s, Volkswagen launched

1046
00:46:44,760 --> 00:46:47,600
一款初代高尔夫敞篷版。
a version of their Mark 1 Golf convertible.

1047
00:46:47,640 --> 00:46:50,120
粉色车漆，配白色真皮内饰，懂吧？
Pink, white leather, okay?

1048
00:46:50,160 --> 00:46:52,520
他们居然管它叫“俏公子”（The Fancy Boy）。
（其实是个都市传说）
And they called it "The Fancy Boy."
(This is an urban legend)

1049
00:46:52,560 --> 00:46:54,160
真是个天才！
[观众笑声]
Genius!
[AUDIENCE LAUGHING]

1050
00:46:54,200 --> 00:46:55,640
咱们英国当年没引进这车，对吧？
- 没有。
We didn't get that one in the UK, did we?
- No.

1051
00:46:55,680 --> 00:46:58,280
英国进口商当时直接说了：
“谢谢，不用了。”
The UK importers said,
"No thanks."

1052
00:46:58,320 --> 00:47:00,080
哈，想想也是。
Yeah, funny, that.

1053
00:47:00,120 --> 00:47:02,400
确实。不过TVR以前
起名字那可是一绝。
Exactly. Now, TVR, in the past,
have been very good at names.

1054
00:47:02,440 --> 00:47:03,920
他们出过“地狱犬”（Cerbera）……
- 是啊。
They had the Cerbera...
- Yeah.

1055
00:47:03,960 --> 00:47:07,040
……那是，呃，算是一种狗，神话里的神犬。
...which was ooh, it's a sort of dog,
it's a dog thing.

1056
00:47:07,080 --> 00:47:09,720
后来又有了“喀迈拉”（Chimaera），
也就是母山羊怪。
- 对。
And then they had Chimaera
which is a she-goat.
- Yeah.

1057
00:47:09,760 --> 00:47:12,560
还有“托斯卡纳”（Tuscan），那可是
掌管万物的至高神。
The Tuscan, which was
the Supreme God of Everything.

1058
00:47:12,600 --> 00:47:15,040
结果现在，他们憋出了个“微波炉”。
And now they've come up with the Microwave.

1059
00:47:15,080 --> 00:47:17,600
[观众笑声]
所以，咱们得给它起个更好的。
[AUDIENCE LAUGHING]
So, we've got to do better than that.

1060
00:47:17,640 --> 00:47:20,840
而且我心里已经有个绝妙的主意了。
And I've got the perfect idea.

1061
00:47:20,880 --> 00:47:22,760
准备好了吗？“寡妇制造者”（The Widowmaker）。
Ready? The Widowmaker.

1062
00:47:22,800 --> 00:47:25,840
噢，绝对不行……你哪能给车起名
叫寡妇制造者！太不像话了！
Oh, absolutely... You can't call a car
Widowmaker! That's awful.

1063
00:47:25,880 --> 00:47:28,000
怎么不行？我就起了。
就叫 TVR 寡妇制造者。
I can. I just have.
It's the TVR Widowmaker.

1064
00:47:28,040 --> 00:47:30,200
60年代那款“星式”战斗机，
They called the Starfighter jet
in the '60s,

1065
00:47:30,240 --> 00:47:31,720
当时就被叫做寡妇制造者。
that was a Widowmaker.

1066
00:47:31,760 --> 00:47:34,080
飞行员们排着队争着开，
开一个摔死一个，
Pilots queued up to fly it,
killed themselves,

1067
00:47:34,120 --> 00:47:36,320
接着立马又有人顶上去。
所有人都挤破头想飞。
and then another one took their seat.
Everyone wanted to fly it.

1068
00:47:36,360 --> 00:47:38,320
不行……不过我懂你的意思了。
You can't... but I know
where you're going, though.

1069
00:47:38,360 --> 00:47:42,160
得是那种霸气威猛的，
比如，TVR“世界末日”（Armageddon），或者……
It needs to be that sort of forceful,
like, TVR Armageddon, or...

1070
00:47:42,200 --> 00:47:44,520
嚯，“末日”听着真不错。
现场还有谁有主意吗？
Ooh, Armageddon's really nice.
Anyone else got any ideas?

1071
00:47:44,560 --> 00:47:46,400
男观众1：波塞冬。
- 波塞冬。
MAN 1: Poseidon.
- Poseidon.

1072
00:47:46,440 --> 00:47:47,960
我挺喜欢的。
- 波塞冬挺不错。
Quite like that.
- Quite like Poseidon.

1073
00:47:48,000 --> 00:47:50,400
他是管什么的来着？
男观众1：海神。
What's it the god of?
MAN 1: The sea.

1074
00:47:50,440 --> 00:47:52,040
海神？可真是太贴切了。
The sea? Pertinent.

1075
00:47:52,080 --> 00:47:54,320
还有人有想法吗？
男观众1：他说索尔！
Anyone else got anything?
MAN 1: He said Thor!

1076
00:47:54,360 --> 00:47:55,600
索尔！
- 我喜欢索尔。
Thor!
- I like Thor.

1077
00:47:55,640 --> 00:47:57,680
男观众2：雷神。
- 对，TVR 索尔。
MAN 2: God of thunder.
- Yeah, TVR Thor.

1078
00:47:57,720 --> 00:47:59,440
听着就带点……
男观众3：哈利·波特！
It's got a bit of...
MAN 3: Harry Potter!

1079
00:47:59,480 --> 00:48:02,360
[观众笑声]
[AUDIENCE LAUGHING]

1080
00:48:02,400 --> 00:48:05,000
水平太差了，烂透了。
男观众3：叫巫师！
That's very, very poor.
MAN 3: The Wizard!

1081
00:48:05,040 --> 00:48:06,720
“巫师”，现在又变成巫师了。
The Wizard, now it's a wizard.

1082
00:48:06,760 --> 00:48:09,240
我倒是挺喜欢……挺喜欢
“TVR 哈利·波特”这个名字。
I quite like... I quite like
the TVR Harry Potter.

1083
00:48:09,280 --> 00:48:10,480
[观众笑声]
[AUDIENCE LAUGHING]

1084
00:48:10,520 --> 00:48:12,080
听着还挺有感觉的。
There's something about it.

1085
00:48:12,120 --> 00:48:14,600
就跟“TVR 著名五人组”似的。
It's like the TVR Famous Five.

1086
00:48:14,640 --> 00:48:17,360
或者“TVR 比阿特丽克斯·波特”。
- 伊妮德·布莱顿。
Or the TVR Beatrix Potter.
- Enid Blyton.

1087
00:48:17,400 --> 00:48:19,560
彼得兔。
你个白痴，照这么扯能扯一整天。
Peter the Rabbit.
We could go on forever, you idiot.

1088
00:48:19,600 --> 00:48:21,080
我觉得咱们跑题了。
I think we're missing the point.

1089
00:48:21,120 --> 00:48:23,040
不如叫“帕丁顿熊”！
（冷知识：查查克拉克森小时候的经历）
It's the Paddington Bear!
(Trivia: look up Clarkson's early life)

1090
00:48:23,080 --> 00:48:24,200
噢，这个绝了。
Oh, that's perfect.

1091
00:48:24,240 --> 00:48:25,800
不过呢，我觉得，
But, I think,

1092
00:48:25,840 --> 00:48:28,120
如果不准我
把它叫作“寡妇制造者”，
if I'm not allowed
to call it "Widowmaker",

1093
00:48:28,160 --> 00:48:32,040
那叫“TVR 瓦尔哈拉”怎么样？
how about the TVR Valhalla?

1094
00:48:32,080 --> 00:48:34,000
行啊，那不是维京人……
- 你说“行啊”是什么意思？
Yeah, wasn't that where the Vikings...
- What do you mean "yeah"?

1095
00:48:34,040 --> 00:48:36,160
这……事实上我已经决定了。
讨论到此结束。
That's... In fact, I've decided.
It's the end of the discussion.

1096
00:48:36,200 --> 00:48:38,000
这简直就是酷车墙争吵重演。
- 没错，简直就像酷车大战。
It is like Cool Wall all over again.
- It is. It's like the Cool War.

1097
00:48:38,040 --> 00:48:39,800
我拍板了。大家提的名字都不错，
I've decided. We've heard some great names

1098
00:48:39,840 --> 00:48:42,800
但管它 TVR 官方叫什么，它就叫瓦尔哈拉了。
but this is, whatever
TVR call it, the Valhalla.

1099
00:48:42,840 --> 00:48:44,600
行了，就这么定。
The end. That's it.

1100
00:48:44,640 --> 00:48:45,920
那地方就是维京人死后鬼混的地方，对吧？
That's where the Vikings hung out when
they were dead, isn't it?

1101
00:48:45,960 --> 00:48:47,240
对，维京亡魂的
Yeah, dead Viking

1102
00:48:47,280 --> 00:48:48,960
安葬之地。
- TVR……
burial ground.
- TVR...

1103
00:48:49,000 --> 00:48:50,480
完美。
- 得，没必要争了。
也成吧。
Perfect.
- Well, there's no point arguing.
Fair enough.

1104
00:48:50,520 --> 00:48:52,280
我们搞定了。
[轻笑]
We've sorted it.
[CHUCKLES]

1105
00:48:52,320 --> 00:48:53,760
总算省心了。
That's a relief.

1106
00:48:53,800 --> 00:48:55,400
言归正传，现在该进行
Anyway, now is the time,

1107
00:48:55,440 --> 00:48:57,560
咱们“最速宗教大对决”的第二轮了。
the second coming of our fastest faiths.

1108
00:48:57,600 --> 00:48:59,640
我们来看看现场这帮弟兄
And we're gonna find out
whether any of our chaps here

1109
00:48:59,680 --> 00:49:01,720
到底有没有人能比英国国教会更快。
were quicker than the Church Of England.

1110
00:49:01,740 --> 00:49:03,980
♪ 卡尔·奥尔夫 - 命运女神 ~ 布兰诗歌 ♪
♪ Carl Orff - O Fortuna ~ Carmina Burana ♪

1111
00:49:04,000 --> 00:49:07,000
道威：和我们上一期的
最速宗教对决一样，
DAWE: As with our previous
fastest faith shoot-out,

1112
00:49:07,040 --> 00:49:13,200
比赛用车依然是
一辆 340 匹马力的斯巴鲁拉力赛车。
the race will be run
in a 340 bhp Subaru rally car.

1113
00:49:13,240 --> 00:49:17,280
那么，英国国教会能否继续稳坐赛道霸主的宝座呢？
So, would the Church of England remain
the kings of the track?

1114
00:49:18,600 --> 00:49:21,760
第一个登场，穆斯林选手塔里克。
First to go, Tariq the Muslim.

1115
00:49:21,800 --> 00:49:22,840
……2、1，走起！
...2, 1, go!

1116
00:49:37,800 --> 00:49:40,680
塔里克原本跑得相当漂亮，
Tariq was doing really well,

1117
00:49:40,720 --> 00:49:45,600
但德鲁伊教徒突然召唤出了远古的转向过度之神。
but then the druid summoned up the ancient
gods of oversteer.

1118
00:49:48,200 --> 00:49:49,400
[轮胎尖叫声]
[TYRES SCREECH]

1119
00:49:54,560 --> 00:49:55,880
可不止打了一次转。
Not just one spin there.

1120
00:49:55,920 --> 00:49:57,720
原地甩甜甜圈能加分，对吧？
You do score extra
for doughnuts, don't you?

1121
00:49:57,760 --> 00:49:59,600
[众人大笑]
[ALL LAUGHING]

1122
00:49:59,640 --> 00:50:02,120
道：但塔里克顶住了魔法攻击，
顺利跑完了整圈。
DAWE: But Tariq overcame the wizardry
to finish the lap.

1123
00:50:05,120 --> 00:50:07,360
[轮胎尖叫声]
[TYRES SCREECHING]

1124
00:50:07,400 --> 00:50:09,280
四个轮子全在惨叫。
[笑声]
All four tyres screeching.
[LAUGHING]

1125
00:50:09,320 --> 00:50:10,840
[听不清]
[INDISCERNABLE]

1126
00:50:10,880 --> 00:50:13,120
不过那儿的刹车点
确实挺难把握的。
It is a difficult braking point
over there though.

1127
00:50:13,160 --> 00:50:15,880
讲真，那地方……
一眼望过去路段太长了。
I've got to say, that is...
You get such a long view of it.

1128
00:50:15,920 --> 00:50:17,760
根本没有任何参照物给你找点。
- 没错，完全没有。
There's no mark there for you.
- Yeah, exactly.

1129
00:50:19,040 --> 00:50:20,280
[笑声]
[LAUGHING]

1130
00:50:20,320 --> 00:50:22,280
下一位，亚瑟·潘德拉贡，
Next up, Arthur Pendragon,

1131
00:50:22,320 --> 00:50:24,800
古代与现代德鲁伊教团成员，
member of the Ancient
and Modern Druid Order,

1132
00:50:24,840 --> 00:50:26,840
梅林与角神大祭司，
priest of Merlin and the Horned God,

1133
00:50:26,880 --> 00:50:29,480
战团首领兼龙之女巫集会最高祭司，
battle chieftain, high priest
of the Dragon Coven,

1134
00:50:30,560 --> 00:50:32,400
以及……莫里斯牛津的车主。
and the Morris Oxford driver.

1135
00:50:35,360 --> 00:50:38,160
我那台标致1.9D听起来可没这么大动静。
My Peugeot 1.9D doesn't sound like that.

1136
00:50:38,200 --> 00:50:39,280
我跟你讲。
- 但愿别这样。
I can tell you.
- Let's hope not.

1137
00:50:39,320 --> 00:50:41,040
它零到六十英里加速得花上整整十分钟。
It's 0-60 in 10 minutes.

1138
00:50:41,080 --> 00:50:42,120
[两人大笑]
[BOTH LAUGHING]

1139
00:50:44,680 --> 00:50:46,640
道：在凯尔特诸神的庇佑下，
DAWE: With the Celtic spirits
rooting for him,

1140
00:50:46,680 --> 00:50:48,600
德鲁伊跑出了相当漂亮利落的一圈。
the druid turned in a tidy lap.

1141
00:50:48,640 --> 00:50:51,080
他过弯怎么能那么快？
How did he get round there so quick?

1142
00:50:51,120 --> 00:50:52,760
利维：这就是魔法呗。[笑]
LEVI: That's magic. [LAUGHS]

1143
00:50:57,080 --> 00:51:00,600
接下来是基督复临安息日会的加里。
Gary, the Seventh-Day Adventist, was next.

1144
00:51:00,640 --> 00:51:02,280
但德鲁伊的法术又显灵了。
But yet again the druid had struck.

1145
00:51:02,320 --> 00:51:05,680
这一回，他念咒把车给变小了。
This time, casting a spell
which shrank the car.

1146
00:51:07,080 --> 00:51:08,480
[笑声]
[LAUGHING]

1147
00:51:15,160 --> 00:51:17,480
我能挤进去的，看！
I can do it. Look!

1148
00:51:17,520 --> 00:51:20,120
[笑声]
别挣扎了，根本不可能塞进去。
[LAUGHING]
It's not gonna happen.

1149
00:51:20,160 --> 00:51:21,520
大家有什么妙招吗？
Any suggestions?

1150
00:51:22,560 --> 00:51:23,400
[笑]
[LAUGHS]

1151
00:51:23,440 --> 00:51:24,840
要不你坐进来陪我？
Why don't you sit in with me?

1152
00:51:24,880 --> 00:51:26,920
上车跟我一起跑，
咱俩凑一对儿？
Come round with me
and we'll do it together?

1153
00:51:26,960 --> 00:51:29,000
[笑] 就像领航员那种？
- 对啊。
[LAUGHS] Like kind of
a co-driver thing?
- Yeah.

1154
00:51:29,040 --> 00:51:30,000
没事，肯定没问题的。
No, it'll be fine.

1155
00:51:30,040 --> 00:51:32,520
[众人大笑]
[ALL LAUGHING]

1156
00:51:32,560 --> 00:51:35,560
我太……呃，这么说吧……
I'm too, er, well,
let me just put it this way...

1157
00:51:35,600 --> 00:51:37,560
没错，我男人味太足了，承让。
Yeah, I'm too manly, thank you.

1158
00:51:37,600 --> 00:51:40,760
对这小车来说我块头太大了。
[笑声]
I'm too big for the car.
[LAUGHING]

1159
00:51:40,800 --> 00:51:42,960
道：现在就剩拉斯塔法里教的利维了，
DAWE: That left Levi, the Rastafarian,

1160
00:51:43,000 --> 00:51:45,280
他开始祈求贾神的灵魂显灵。
who called on the spirit of Jah.

1161
00:51:45,320 --> 00:51:48,400
好嘞，赞美真神，神力加持。出发！
Yes, Jah, Might. Let's go.

1162
00:51:48,440 --> 00:51:51,080
而此时，德鲁伊的法术已经见底了。
And by now, the druid was out of spells.

1163
00:51:52,960 --> 00:51:54,440
[引擎轰鸣加速]
[ENGINE ACCELERATING]

1164
00:52:03,320 --> 00:52:05,360
终于来了一位像样的劲敌，
And at last, a proper rival

1165
00:52:05,400 --> 00:52:08,000
足以挑战来自英国国教会的
现任冠军。
to the current champion
from the Church Of England.

1166
00:52:08,040 --> 00:52:11,280
因为和他一样，奥莱维也是个
周末跑赛道的业余玩家。
Because like him, OLevi's
an amateur weekend racer.

1167
00:52:12,920 --> 00:52:14,320
水平确实一眼便知。
And it showed.

1168
00:52:14,360 --> 00:52:16,080
[轮胎尖叫]
[TYRES SCREECHING]

1169
00:52:21,120 --> 00:52:25,040
全都是超级巨星，
可这场面简直是彻头彻尾的悲剧。
Superstars, one and all,
and what a complete tragedy.

1170
00:52:25,080 --> 00:52:26,800
是啊，那车实在太小了。
Yeah, the car was too small.

1171
00:52:26,840 --> 00:52:28,960
[笑]
兄弟，我太懂那种滋味了。
- 是啊。
[LAUGHS]
I know the feeling, mate.
- Yeah.

1172
00:52:29,000 --> 00:52:30,760
所有的车对咱们来说都太小了，对吧？
All cars are too small, aren't they?

1173
00:52:30,800 --> 00:52:33,000
我可体会不到那种滋味。
[众人大笑]
I don't know that feeling.
[ALL LAUGHING]

1174
00:52:33,040 --> 00:52:35,960
我从来没受过这方面的罪。
[笑]
It's not one I suffer from.
[LAUGHS]

1175
00:52:36,000 --> 00:52:37,920
凭啥我非得站这儿？
- 赶紧公布成绩吧。
Why do I have to stand here?
- Let's do the results.

1176
00:52:37,960 --> 00:52:40,400
好嘞，走起。按照老规矩，
倒序揭晓，
Right, here we go. In reverse order,
as is traditional,

1177
00:52:40,440 --> 00:52:43,120
第四名嘛，[笑]
非你莫属了，加里，
in fourth place, [LAUGHS]
that'll be you, Gary,

1178
00:52:43,160 --> 00:52:45,160
因为你压根连车都塞不进去。
- 行吧。
because you couldn't get in the car.
- Okay.

1179
00:52:45,200 --> 00:52:47,680
你目前的用时成绩，
大概是四小时。
You scored a time of so far,
about four hours.

1180
00:52:47,720 --> 00:52:49,080
[笑]
哈蒙德：挺好。
[LAUGHS]
HAMMOND: Very well.

1181
00:52:49,120 --> 00:52:50,360
别往心里去。
Not to worry.

1182
00:52:50,400 --> 00:52:52,880
第三名——亚瑟王，
Third place - King Arthur,

1183
00:52:52,920 --> 00:52:57,280
其实也算是在意料之中，
成绩是1分48秒。
kind of predictably really,
with a time of 1:48.

1184
00:52:57,320 --> 00:52:59,520
第二名，塔里克，
In second place, Tariq,

1185
00:52:59,560 --> 00:53:02,080
相当不错的成绩，1分41秒。
- 多谢。
with a very good time, 1:41.
- Thank you.

1186
00:53:02,120 --> 00:53:04,000
现在，重头戏来了，
Now, the big question is,

1187
00:53:04,040 --> 00:53:06,320
此时此刻我们已经知道，
we know at this point that

1188
00:53:06,360 --> 00:53:09,480
拉斯塔法里教的
奥莱维·多克特罗夫拔得头筹，
the Rastafarian,
OLevi Doctrove, has won

1189
00:53:09,520 --> 00:53:11,440
但最大的悬念在于，
but the big question is,

1190
00:53:11,480 --> 00:53:14,280
你到底有没有干翻英国国教会？
- 嗯。
have you beaten the Church Of England?
- Mmm.

1191
00:53:14,320 --> 00:53:17,200
当年他们来这儿跑了一圈，
用时1分37秒，
Now when they came here, they went around
in one minute, 37 seconds,

1192
00:53:17,240 --> 00:53:18,880
比你们这帮人都快。
faster than all you lot.

1193
00:53:18,920 --> 00:53:23,200
而你跑完这一圈，用了1分31秒！
- 芜湖！
You went round in one minute, 31 seconds.
- Whoo!

1194
00:53:23,240 --> 00:53:25,480
[欢呼与口哨声]
[CHEERING AND WHISTLING]

1195
00:53:28,120 --> 00:53:29,640
简直跑得太绝了！
That was fantastic!

1196
00:53:30,400 --> 00:53:31,720
这成绩仅仅……
That's only...

1197
00:53:33,520 --> 00:53:35,240
这居然仅仅……
That is only...

1198
00:53:35,280 --> 00:53:36,600
哎呀，比起斯提格创下的标杆圈速，
Well, it's less than two seconds

1199
00:53:36,640 --> 00:53:38,440
只落后了不到两秒。
off the pace set by The Stig.

1200
00:53:38,480 --> 00:53:40,160
这表现简直不可思议！
That's an unbelievable performance.

1201
00:53:40,200 --> 00:53:41,800
杰森，把奖杯拿上来。
Jason, bring in the trophy.

1202
00:53:41,840 --> 00:53:44,280
给您，“跑得最快的宗教”。
There you are, the fastest faith.

1203
00:53:44,320 --> 00:53:46,240
谢谢。
Thank you.

1204
00:53:49,440 --> 00:53:51,640
[交头接耳]
[INDISTINCT CONVERSATION]

1205
00:53:53,920 --> 00:53:56,880
好吧，说实话，
目前来看确实是最快的宗教，
Well, actually,
it's the fastest faith for now

1206
00:53:56,920 --> 00:54:00,320
除非我们能找到一个
体型更小的基督复临安息日会教徒。
[笑声]
unless we can find
a smaller Seventh-Day Adventist.
[LAUGHS]

1207
00:54:00,360 --> 00:54:02,560
要么换辆更大的车！
- 没错。
Or a bigger car!
- Yep.

1208
00:54:02,600 --> 00:54:03,880
言归正传，每周我们都会请一位明星
Anyway, every week, we put a star

1209
00:54:03,920 --> 00:54:06,200
来开开我们的廉价车，对吧？
in a reasonably priced car. Okay?

1210
00:54:06,240 --> 00:54:08,320
这一整季我们都是这么干的。
We've done that throughout the series.

1211
00:54:08,360 --> 00:54:11,360
这些人的表现嘛……可谓是良莠不齐。
And they've been a mixed bag.

1212
00:54:11,400 --> 00:54:13,280
女士们先生们，哈里·恩菲尔德！
♪ 黑色安息日 - Paranoid ♪
Ladies and gentlemen, Harry Enfield!
♪ Black Sabbath - Paranoid ♪

1213
00:54:13,320 --> 00:54:15,360
希望我别丧命，各就各位，预备，跑！哇啊！
Hope I don't die, ready, steady, go. Whagh!

1214
00:54:16,640 --> 00:54:20,200
手刹甩尾。时速飙到30英里了。
Handbrake skid. Up onto 30mph.

1215
00:54:20,240 --> 00:54:22,160
呀啊啊！
Yahhh!

1216
00:54:22,200 --> 00:54:24,360
好吧，刚才那下我失控了。
Okay, I lost control of that.

1217
00:54:24,400 --> 00:54:26,440
杰米罗奎尔乐队主唱，杰·凯！
Jamiroquai front man, Jay Kay!

1218
00:54:28,000 --> 00:54:29,560
稳住别失误。
Don't be punished.

1219
00:54:29,600 --> 00:54:32,000
千万别忍不住猛踩油门。
Don't be tempted to put too much power on.

1220
00:54:32,040 --> 00:54:33,880
太漂亮了。
That's beautiful.

1221
00:54:33,920 --> 00:54:35,320
[轮胎嘶鸣]
[TYRES SCREECHING]

1222
00:54:37,560 --> 00:54:39,520
[轮胎嘶鸣]
[TYRES SCREECHING]

1223
00:54:39,560 --> 00:54:41,200
[笑声]
[LAUGHS]

1224
00:54:44,160 --> 00:54:45,720
罗斯·坎普！
Ross Kemp!

1225
00:54:48,040 --> 00:54:49,400
[轮胎嘶鸣]
[TYRES SCREECHING]

1226
00:54:50,480 --> 00:54:51,720
烂透了！
Rubbish!

1227
00:54:51,760 --> 00:54:54,520
我恨你。我简直恨死你了，克拉克森。
I hate you. I hate you so much, Clarkson.

1228
00:54:54,560 --> 00:54:55,960
总有一天
我会找你报仇的，等着瞧。
I'm gonna get you back
at some point, you know.

1229
00:54:56,000 --> 00:54:57,360
乔纳森·罗斯！
Jonathan Ross!

1230
00:54:57,400 --> 00:54:59,440
看看这华丽的过弯！
Look at that magnificent turn!

1231
00:54:59,480 --> 00:55:01,080
克拉克森：才不华丽呢。
CLARKSON: It wasn't.

1232
00:55:01,120 --> 00:55:03,360
到这儿，我觉得我得从那头绕过去。
At this bit, I think I have to go
round the end.

1233
00:55:03,400 --> 00:55:05,800
克拉克森：你看起来蠢透了！[笑声]
CLARKSON: You look ridiculous! [LAUGHS]

1234
00:55:09,720 --> 00:55:11,640
我看着活像个《星际迷航》死宅粉。
I look like a Star Trek fan.

1235
00:55:14,320 --> 00:55:16,400
[观众大笑]
[AUDIENCE LAUGHING]

1236
00:55:17,520 --> 00:55:19,720
我还活着算你走运。
You're lucky I'm still alive.

1237
00:55:19,760 --> 00:55:22,000
你觉得我会在乎吗？
- 不在乎，但你确实算走运。
Do you think I care?
- No, but you're lucky.

1238
00:55:22,040 --> 00:55:24,760
谁想看看他练习时的那些糗样？
Who'd like to see some of the practices
that he had?

1239
00:55:25,960 --> 00:55:27,960
[观众大笑]
[AUDIENCE LAUGHING]

1240
00:55:28,000 --> 00:55:30,640
我当时以为那么开会更快点嘛。
[笑声]
I thought it might be faster.
[LAUGHS]

1241
00:55:31,800 --> 00:55:33,680
女士们先生们，史蒂夫·库根！
Ladies and gentlemen, Steve Coogan!

1242
00:55:35,640 --> 00:55:36,960
还好我提前刷过牙了！
I'm glad I cleaned me teeth!

1243
00:55:37,000 --> 00:55:39,120
恐惧感正在逐渐累积，
There's a gradual build-up of terror

1244
00:55:39,160 --> 00:55:41,440
瞧这脸上的架势。
一开始只是轻微恐慌。
by the looks of things.
Start with mild panic.

1245
00:55:41,480 --> 00:55:43,240
这把走线挺利落。
That's quite neat.

1246
00:55:45,040 --> 00:55:46,680
[模仿角色口音]
“我开的是雷克萨斯湿！”
[IN CHARACTER]
"I drive a Lexush!"

1247
00:55:46,720 --> 00:55:49,400
53秒！罗斯·坎普绝对要气疯了。
53! Ross Kemp's gonna be so angry.

1248
00:55:49,440 --> 00:55:51,240
我干掉了罗斯·坎普！
I beat Ross Kemp!

1249
00:55:51,280 --> 00:55:52,920
塔拉·帕尔默-汤姆金森。
Tara Palmer-Tomkinson.

1250
00:55:52,960 --> 00:55:54,440
我快杀到哈维·尼克斯百货了。
I'm coming up to Harvey Nichols.

1251
00:55:54,480 --> 00:55:55,840
商场眼看就要关门了。
And the shop is about to close.

1252
00:55:57,080 --> 00:55:58,200
[轮胎尖叫声]
[TYRES SCREECH]

1253
00:55:58,240 --> 00:55:59,880
全速狂飙！
I'm blasting.

1254
00:55:59,920 --> 00:56:01,440
噢，街上有个帅哥，冲他招招手。
Oh. Sexy man on the street, wave to him.

1255
00:56:01,480 --> 00:56:02,760
[大笑]
- 往左。
[LAUGHING]
- Left.

1256
00:56:05,440 --> 00:56:07,320
我从不撞车，但停车的时候嘛，
I don't crash, but when I park

1257
00:56:07,360 --> 00:56:11,480
我觉得保险杠不就是用来
“砰、砰、砰，进位”的嘛。
I think that the bumpers are there so
you go, "Bump, bump, bump, in."

1258
00:56:11,520 --> 00:56:14,280
来自Status Quo乐队的里克·帕菲特！
From Status Quo, Rick Parfitt!

1259
00:56:14,320 --> 00:56:15,720
噢，惨了！
[观众大笑]
Oh, no!
[AUDIENCE LAUGHING]

1260
00:56:17,640 --> 00:56:19,400
漂亮……噢不，还没完呢。
Beautiful... oh, no, there's more.

1261
00:56:19,440 --> 00:56:21,240
八成吓得屁都崩出来了。
Probably broke wind.

1262
00:56:21,280 --> 00:56:22,680
克拉克森：重回赛道。
CLARKSON: Back on.

1263
00:56:23,080 --> 00:56:24,720
[笑声]
[LAUGHS]

1264
00:56:24,760 --> 00:56:26,880
[众人大笑]
[ALL LAUGHING]

1265
00:56:26,920 --> 00:56:29,760
克拉克森：横着滑过了终点线。
CLARKSON: Across the line sideways.

1266
00:56:29,800 --> 00:56:32,120
女士们先生们，迈克尔·甘本爵士！
Ladies and gentlemen, Sir Michael Gambon!

1267
00:56:32,160 --> 00:56:34,400
[引擎轰鸣]
[ENGINE REVVING]

1268
00:56:34,440 --> 00:56:36,560
你看着确实吓得够呛。
You do look quite scared.

1269
00:56:38,000 --> 00:56:39,640
轮胎堆！天呐！
Tyres! God!

1270
00:56:40,880 --> 00:56:43,120
你刚才离轮胎墙太近了。
You were very close
to the tyres there.

1271
00:56:43,160 --> 00:56:45,040
本来就该贴着过。
- 是啊，不过刚才本来挺漂亮……
You're supposed to be.
- Yeah, well, that was beautifully...

1272
00:56:45,080 --> 00:56:46,280
其实，你冲出……
Actually, you're off the...

1273
00:56:46,320 --> 00:56:48,520
[观众大笑]
[AUDIENCE LAUGHING]

1274
00:56:48,560 --> 00:56:51,280
你撞上——
哇呼呼呼呼！
You've hit-
Whoo-hoo-hoo-hoo!

1275
00:56:52,000 --> 00:56:53,440
[掌声]
[APPLAUDING]

1276
00:56:56,080 --> 00:56:57,800
戈登·拉姆齐。
Gordon Ramsay.

1277
00:56:57,840 --> 00:56:59,480
见鬼！我敢发誓
刚才看见了个抄牌的交警。
Bloody hell! I could have sworn
I just saw a traffic warden.

1278
00:56:59,520 --> 00:57:01,400
[观众大笑]
[AUDIENCE LAUGHING]

1279
00:57:01,440 --> 00:57:05,040
这玩意儿一股汽油味。
That tastes of petrol.

1280
00:57:05,080 --> 00:57:08,040
而且这还是在斯巴鲁森林人的
水平对置四缸引擎上烤出来的，
And that was done on the Subaru
Forrester flat-four engine,

1281
00:57:08,080 --> 00:57:09,480
这底子相当扎实。
it's a very good base.

1282
00:57:10,040 --> 00:57:11,200
[笑声]
[LAUGHS]

1283
00:57:13,680 --> 00:57:14,840
[掌声]
[APPLAUDING]

1284
00:57:15,560 --> 00:57:16,600
那么……
Now...

1285
00:57:18,000 --> 00:57:19,720
刚才这段兼具了……
A mixture...

1286
00:57:19,760 --> 00:57:23,000
兼具了从容、精准，
以及哈利·恩菲尔德式的搞笑。
A mixture of poise, precision
and Harry Enfield there.

1287
00:57:23,040 --> 00:57:25,440
但现在该颁发大奖了，
But now it's time to award the prize

1288
00:57:25,480 --> 00:57:27,920
颁给整季节目中
车速最快的名人。
to the fastest celebrity
in the whole series.

1289
00:57:27,960 --> 00:57:30,160
看看我们这个成绩板，获胜者是——
And it was, if we look on this board,

1290
00:57:30,200 --> 00:57:32,240
成绩为1分48秒的 Jay Kay！
Jay Kay with a time of 1:48,

1291
00:57:32,280 --> 00:57:34,120
各位，他今天也来到现场了！
and he's here, everybody!

1292
00:57:34,160 --> 00:57:35,480
[欢呼与口哨声]
[CHEERING AND WHISTLING]

1293
00:57:39,040 --> 00:57:41,320
干得漂亮！
Well done!

1294
00:57:41,360 --> 00:57:43,240
天哪。
- 我知道是谁了。
God.
- I know who it is.

1295
00:57:43,280 --> 00:57:45,360
天哪，旁边都碎了一块。
God. It's broken on the side.

1296
00:57:45,400 --> 00:57:48,000
那头掉了一块下来，
我得道个歉。
I should apologise for the end
that's come off there.

1297
00:57:48,040 --> 00:57:50,720
BBC 这次可真是“下了血本”啊。
The BBC has really
pushed the boat out.

1298
00:57:50,760 --> 00:57:52,480
稍微摔烂了点。你想发表
一下获奖感言吗？
Slightly broke. Would you
like to make a speech?

1299
00:57:52,520 --> 00:57:56,280
来一段汤姆·汉克斯风格的
领奖感言就挺不错。
A little Tom Hanks style
acceptance speech would be good.

1300
00:57:56,320 --> 00:57:59,120
不用了，没事。
- 我只想跟大伙说一句，呃……
No, it's okay.
- I'd just like to say
to everybody that, erm,

1301
00:57:59,160 --> 00:58:01,400
拿到这个……呃……
算是我人生中最辉煌的日子之一了。
it's one of the greatest days of my life
to get this, er...

1302
00:58:01,440 --> 00:58:02,480
[观众笑声]
[AUDIENCE LAUGHING]

1303
00:58:02,520 --> 00:58:04,440
能拿到这个奖项。
To get this award.

1304
00:58:04,480 --> 00:58:06,320
而且，呃，你知道的，全英音乐奖还是格莱美奖，
And, er, you know, no Brit award or Grammy

1305
00:58:06,360 --> 00:58:07,640
都压根没法跟这个比。
could come close to that.

1306
00:58:07,680 --> 00:58:09,760
我只想感谢杰里米，感谢BBC，
And I just wanna thank Jeremy, the BBC,

1307
00:58:09,800 --> 00:58:11,680
感谢上帝，感谢老妈，感谢大家。非常感谢！
God, Mum, everybody. Thank you very much.

1308
00:58:11,720 --> 00:58:12,680
太棒了！
Fantastic!

1309
00:58:17,880 --> 00:58:19,240
那么……
And that...

1310
00:58:19,280 --> 00:58:21,560
恐怕今天节目的时间
就全部用光了。
And that, I'm afraid,
is all we've got time for.

1311
00:58:21,600 --> 00:58:23,800
我们明年春天再见。
We will be back in the spring.

1312
00:58:23,840 --> 00:58:26,280
不过在此期间，
祝大家假期过得愉快。
But in the meantime,
have a very happy holiday.

1313
00:58:26,320 --> 00:58:28,400
再见！拜拜！
（再见，杰森！）
Goodbye! Bye!
(Bye Jason!)

1314
00:58:28,440 --> 00:58:30,520
挥挥手，斯提格，挥挥手！
Wave, Stig, wave!

1315
00:58:30,560 --> 00:58:31,800
挥手啊！
Wave!

1316
00:58:31,840 --> 00:58:33,640
[片尾主题曲响起]
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

